l be the only Net Zero  metallurgical cooking coal mine in the  world  [Applause]  and it is vitally important that all of  us recognize  as the inspector does on page 255 that  the proposed development would to some  extent support the transition to a  low-carbon future is specifically as a  consequence of the provision of a  currently needed resource from a mine  that aspires to be Net Zero I think it  is also important that we recognize that  in any change of uh land use there will  always be a potential impact on  biodiversity and on the local  environment as well and again it is  important to denote that the inspector  on page 278 of his uh report makes it  clear that this mind would not cause any  unacceptable impacts on ecology nor  result in a net loss in biodiversity  uh and they expect to also makes clear  in paragraph 22.9 that the Pro's  development itself would have an overall  neutral effect on climate change and as  such there would be no material conflict  with government policies for meeting the  challenge of climate change  a report from England's chief medical  officer has found that eco-designed wood  burning stoves produce 450 times more  toxic air pollution than gas Central  Heating and to Chris witty's report  found that older heat is now banned from  sale produced nearly 4 000 times more  air pollution while electric heating  produces none  Professor which is report also calls on  people to have the courage to tell  motorists to stop idling engines as part  of efforts to tackle pollution air  pollution was chosen by circus as the  focus of his 2022 annual report he said  there has been progress in tackling  outdoor air pollution over the years and  that is set to continue but outdoor air  pollution still leads to between 26 and  38 000 deaths a year in England alone  Rising temperatures driven by climate  breakdown are causing distress to the  fetuses of pregnant Farmers a study  revealed the fetuses of women working in  fields in The Gambia 